# Working method

cha.mdc holds the hard repo constraints and is authoritative. If anything
here or in any other rule file appears to conflict with cha.mdc, cha.mdc
wins. Say so rather than resolving it silently.

This file covers only how to work, not what the constraints are.

## Inspect before proposing

- Read the actual files first. Never propose an edit based on an
  assumption about what a file contains.
- Find files yourself with search. Do not ask the user to paste code you
  are able to read. The user is a domain expert and a beginner with dev
  tools; every manual step you push onto them is a cost.
- If the request is ambiguous, name the ambiguity and ask one question.
  Do not guess and proceed.

## Before declaring done

- Read your own diff with git diff main...HEAD and check it against the
  constraints, including files you did not intend to touch.
- Never leave a TODO, a stub or partial work. If you are blocked, stop
  and say exactly what blocks you.
- Never install a dependency without asking first.

## Generated data

data/plans/*.json and data/plan-index.json are built output. Never
hand-edit them. Change scripts/build-plan-profiles.js and rebuild.
